# The assistant benchmark's ontology snapshots are kept byte for byte: each case records the
# SHA-256 of the file it was generated from (line endings normalised, so a CRLF checkout still
# matches), but the snapshot itself should be exactly the file the cases were made from.
benchmarks/assistant/ontologies/*.owl -text

# ODK's own templates, copied out of the ODK image, and the goldens made in that image. A project
# OntoBoard creates must equal what `odk.py seed` writes byte for byte, and these are what that is
# rendered from and compared with - so git must not touch their line endings. With
# core.autocrlf=true and without these lines a Windows checkout turns every one of them into CRLF.
protege-plugin/src/main/odk/** -text
protege-plugin/src/test/resources/odk/** -text
